  message: "Fixed in PR #2347 (stable-id scheme v18, owner ruling of 2026-11-23 above). Two-layout fixture pairs re-run on dev 49bc5c6e4, stable ids differing between the layouts: point 1: cuda 0 of 10, d 0 of 16 and 0 of 3, zig 0 of 11, haxe 0 of 9, odin 0 of 7, objc 0 of 12. Point 2: typescript 0 of 11; the fix is in the JavaScript/TypeScript hashed text, and the filed function-level repro layout_free('(x:\\n  & A\\n  & B)', separators=True) still returns '(x: &A & B)' because that function stays language-blind (a Rust &self after a line break). Point 3: haskell 0 of 7, ocaml 0 of 5, fsharp 0 of 10, 0 of 10, 0 of 8, agda 0 of 7. Point 4: whitespace inside a regex default value is kept as meaning (packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_jsts_hashed_text_layout.py). Point 5 (one language-blind spacing choice per token): DECIDED, leave it. A per-language table was measured offline and would move koel 111 of 3,201 PHP typed ids for no id that is wrong today; the owner can overturn this. Point 6: groovy 0 of 9, julia 0 of 7, solidity 0 of 16, javascript 0 of 11 on dev 49bc5c6e4; rust_scip with rust-analyzer was measured by the build (0 of 14) and not re-run by me on dev. Beyond the six points, untyped names, scope labels and attribute text are now hashed without layout in every language except the content-name languages; that moved 257 declared stable ids over 42 repositories (Makefile 153, TypeScript 76, CMake 10, CUDA 10, Handlebars 4, Go 3, Clojure 1). NOT fixed and filed as WI-radim-najar-juhob-pisab-zovuz-gijof-vifap-jajin: table-formula and doc-formula names (the Vue pair still differs, 2 of 10, on dev 49bc5c6e4). Outputs: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/closure/ (fixtures*.txt, trees_summary.txt, pair_check_dev.txt)."  # c59a
